---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import { release, releaseURL } from '../../data/site';
---

<Site
  title="Configra — Configuration and sensitive-value management | Viber Ops"
  description="Manage YAML, JSON, sensitive values and client certificates. Applications read configuration through the Go SDK, CSI files or native Kubernetes objects."
  section="products"
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="product-hero container">
      <div class="product-kicker">
        <span class="mini-mark">c</span>
        <span>Configra</span>
        <a class="tag" href={releaseURL}>
          {release} · Preview
        </a>
      </div>
      <h1>
        Manage application
        <br />
        <span>configuration and secrets.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="product-intro">
        YAML, JSON, passwords and certificate files for each environment.
        <br class="desktop-break" />
        Read them through the Go SDK, mounted files or native Secret / ConfigMap objects.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/en/docs/configra/quickstart/">
          Get started →
        </a>
        <a class="button button-outline" href="/en/docs/configra/installation/">
          Download for macOS / Linux
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/viber-ops/configra">
          View source ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <span>Self-hosted</span>
        <span>YAML / JSON</span>
        <span>Go SDK</span>
        <span>Two Kubernetes modes</span>
      </div>
      <figure class="workspace-shot">
        <div class="shot-header">
          <span>CONFIGRA / VAULT</span>
          <span>Items, environment variants and revision history</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/assets/configra/vault-light.png" aria-label="Open the full Vault screenshot">
          <img
            src="/assets/configra/vault-light.png"
            width="1440"
            height="1000"
            alt="Configra Vault workspace showing a database item, environment variants, field references and revision history."
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Actual UI · Demo data · Sensitive values hidden by default</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="section container use-cases">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">USE CASES</p>
        <h2>When is Configra useful?</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>
          You copy environment-specific configuration between repositories, scripts and clusters.
        </li>
        <li>
          Several configurations share passwords or certificate files that you want to reference
          instead of duplicate.
        </li>
        <li>
          Developers need configuration reads; operators need revision history and credential
          management.
        </li>
        <li>
          Some applications can use an SDK, while others only read files or environment variables.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="feature-section">
      <div class="container section">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">INTEGRATIONS</p>
            <h2>Three ways to connect applications</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Go applications can use the SDK.
            <br />
            Other applications can read files or environment variables.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="delivery-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="index-label">GO SDK</span>
            <h3>Read resolved configuration</h3>
            <p>
              Fetch YAML / JSON with the Go SDK. The Viper Handler adds ETag polling and an
              in-memory last-known-good snapshot.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/go-sdk/">
              Use the Go SDK →
            </a>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="index-label">CSI PROVIDER</span>
            <h3>Mount files into a Pod</h3>
            <p>
              The Secrets Store CSI provider mounts Configs and File fields. Driver rotation updates
              files; your application reloads them.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/kubernetes/#csi-file-mounts">
              Set up the CSI provider →
            </a>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="index-label">KUBERNETES SYNC</span>
            <h3>Sync to a Secret or ConfigMap</h3>
            <p>
              Use native volumes or envFrom. Volume updates follow Kubernetes behavior;
              environment-variable changes require Pod replacement.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/kubernetes/#native-object-sync">
              Use native synchronization →
            </a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section container capabilities">
      <div class="capability-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">CONFIGS & VAULT</p>
        <h2>Reference Vault fields in configuration</h2>
        <p>
          Configra resolves current field values for the requested environment. Applications receive
          the complete document.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Manage configuration and field variants by environment</li>
          <li>Inspect history, compare changes and clone configuration</li>
          <li>Explicitly reveal or conceal sensitive values</li>
          <li>Investigate reads and changes through Access and Audit</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/configuration/">
          Read about Configs and Vault →
        </a>
      </div>
      <a
        class="detail-shot"
        href="/assets/configra/vault-dark.png"
        aria-label="Open the dark workspace screenshot"
      >
        <img
          src="/assets/configra/vault-dark.png"
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          alt="Configra dark workspace with Vault fields and revision navigation."
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </a>
    </section>
    <section class="section container credential-section">
      <div class="credential-image">
        <a href="/assets/configra/authorities.png" aria-label="Open the client CA screenshot">
          <img
            src="/assets/configra/authorities.png"
            width="1280"
            height="750"
            alt="Administration lists managed client certificate authorities with issuance and revocation controls."
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">CLIENT CERTIFICATES</p>
        <h2>Create CAs and issue client certificates</h2>
        <p>
          Generate a CA and issue client identities in the workspace. CA signing keys are retained
          encrypted; private exports are returned only with the original creation response.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/certificates/">
          Manage client certificates →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="boundary-note container">
      <span class="tag">Before deployment</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Permission scope and release status</h3>
        <p>
          Machine Tokens grant Environment-wide access, not per-resource isolation. Configra does
          not provide dynamic database credentials, HSM/KMS custody or application restarts. This is
          a preview release; production performance acceptance is incomplete.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/en/docs/configra/security/">
          Read the security and release status →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="docs-banner container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">QUICKSTART</p>
        <h2>Run Configra locally</h2>
        <p>Use the development stack to explore the UI, create configuration and test reads.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-light" href="/en/docs/configra/quickstart/">
        Open the quickstart →
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>
